  limitations: "Only decoded_len, encoded_len and From<Error> for core::fmt::Error are covered; general Display formatting is not proved. Hexadecimal encoding, decoding, character validation, destination writes, allocation and encode_str's unchecked UTF-8 conversion are not verified. encoded_len behavior above usize::MAX / 2 is outside the proved precondition. Other targets, feature configurations and release overflow behavior were not checked. The separate Display supplement covers only default formatting and this fixed writer, not arbitrary format flags/writers, partial-prefix error policies, other targets or feature configurations. It adds no Aeneas mapping. Encoded-length overflow remains outside the existing precondition." -> "Only decoded_len, encoded_len and From<Error> for core::fmt::Error are covered; general Display formatting is not proved. General-length hexadecimal encoding, decoding, character validation, destination writes, allocation and encode_str's unchecked UTF-8 conversion are not verified. encoded_len behavior above usize::MAX / 2 is outside the proved precondition. Other targets, feature configurations and release overflow behavior were not checked. The separate Display supplement covers only default formatting and this fixed writer, not arbitrary format flags/writers, partial-prefix error policies, other targets or feature configurations. It adds no Aeneas mapping. Encoded-length overflow remains outside the existing precondition. These five codec checks cover only source/destination lengths2/3 for decode and1/4 for encode, with independent1-byte roundtrip decode destinations. They do not prove arbitrary lengths/capacities, general failure-side prefix contents, encode_str UTF8 conversion, allocation or encoded_len overflow. Ordinary Kani supplements add no Aeneas mappings."
